# Forbidden patterns for Kotlin files (*.kt, *.kts). Applied by .githooks/pre-commit.
# scaffold-extensions: kt kts
# Format: <regex><TAB><description>   (one per line; # comments ignored)
# Separator is TAB - patterns can contain literal `|` for ERE alternation; no literal TAB.
# Copy to your project as `.forbidden-patterns/kotlin.txt`.
# Note: *.kts are Gradle/script files where println() is idiomatic; flagging it there
# still catches stray debug output, but expect to scaffold-allow legitimate cases.
# print/println/TODO anchors exclude a preceding `.` so member calls like writer.println(),
# document.print(), and obj.TODO() do NOT match - only the unqualified kotlin.io builtins do.

(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_.])println[[:space:]]*\(	Use the project's logger (e.g. slf4j/kotlin-logging), not println()
(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_.])print[[:space:]]*\(	Use the project's logger, not print()
System\.(out|err)\.print(ln)?[[:space:]]*\(	Use the project's logger, not System.out/System.err.print(ln)
(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])printStackTrace[[:space:]]*\(	Log the exception via the project's logger, not printStackTrace()
(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_.])TODO[[:space:]]*\(	kotlin.TODO() throws NotImplementedError at runtime - finish the impl or open a ticket

# --- Security: JVM RCE / reflection / TLS sinks (java.txt's rules, Kotlin syntax) ---
# Kotlin reaches the same JVM sinks and has no linter, hook lint or real CI job
# here either. There is no `new` keyword, so the constructor rule anchors on the
# bare call; readObject is matched in its NO-ARG form only.
# checkServerTrusted is matched ONLY with an EMPTY BODY on the same line - the
# `{}` (or `= Unit`) of the copy-pasted trust-all TrustManager. A real implementation (body on
# the following lines) and a `delegate.checkServerTrusted(...)` call do not fire;
# an empty body split across two lines is not seen (line-at-a-time scan).
# setAccessible/isAccessible are NOT active rules - see the opt-in block below.
(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])ObjectInputStream[[:space:]]*\(	Java deserialization of untrusted bytes is RCE (CVE-2015-4852 class) - use JSON/protobuf with a schema
\.readObject[[:space:]]*\([[:space:]]*\)	ObjectInputStream.readObject() on untrusted input is RCE - deserialize a schema-checked format instead
(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])Runtime\.getRuntime[[:space:]]*\([[:space:]]*\)[[:space:]]*\.exec	Runtime.exec() is a command-injection sink - use ProcessBuilder with a fixed argv
(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])checkServerTrusted[[:space:]]*\([^)]*\)([^{]*\{[[:space:]]*\}|[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*Unit)	An EMPTY checkServerTrusted() accepts every certificate - that is TLS validation switched off (MITM risk); validate the chain or keep the platform TrustManager
ALLOW_ALL_HOSTNAME_VERIFIER	ALLOW_ALL_HOSTNAME_VERIFIER disables TLS hostname checking (MITM risk) - keep the default verifier

# Optional (opt-in) — uncomment a line to enable it:
# (^|[^A-Za-z_])(TODO|FIXME|XXX)($|[^A-Za-z0-9_])	TODO/FIXME/XXX comment not allowed - open a ticket instead (FP-prone in comments/strings)
# @Disabled($|[^A-Za-z0-9_])	Disabled JUnit5 test committed - re-enable or delete (may be intentional)
# (^|[^A-Za-z_])(it|i)gnore[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true	Ignored test annotation - re-enable or delete (FP-prone; matches config flags)
# !![[:space:]]*($|[^=])	Avoid the !! not-null assertion - use safe calls or requireNotNull (very FP-prone)
# GlobalScope\.	Avoid GlobalScope - use a structured-concurrency CoroutineScope (some scripts legitimately use it)
# setAccessible/isAccessible ship OFF: a design smell, not a sink, and routine in
# framework glue and test helpers. `isAccessible` is also an ordinary property
# name, so the opt-in form below is anchored to `.isAccessible =` - that keeps
# `Room(name = "Lab", isAccessible = true)` and `r.copy(isAccessible = true)`
# quiet, but `view.isAccessible = true` (Android) still fires once enabled.
# (\.setAccessible[[:space:]]*\([[:space:]]*true[[:space:]]*\)|\.isAccessible[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true)	setAccessible/isAccessible = true defeats access control and final-field safety - drop the reflection (off by default: routine in framework glue and tests)
